  17:     Slide each loose pixel until it touches the full bar with the same color, deleting unmatched pixels.
  18: 
  19:     Input structure:
  20:     - The input contains full horizontal or vertical bars and single colored pixels on black.
  21:     - Bars are monochromatic and span the full height or width.
  22:     - Some loose pixels share colors with bars and some may not.
  23: 
  24:     Rule:
  25:     - Copy all bars unchanged to the output.
  26:     - For each loose pixel with a matching-color bar, slide it in a cardinal direction until it contacts that bar.
  27:     - Drop any loose pixel whose color has no corresponding bar.
  28: 
  29:     Key insight:
  30:     - Bar color is the destination label: matching pixels move until first contact with their same-color
  31:       full-line anchor.
